&lt;h3>hugo.yaml&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="hugoyaml">&lt;/span>
&lt;a href="#hugoyaml" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section">&lt;/a>&lt;/h3>&lt;blockquote>
&lt;p>    Configure your site using files, directories, and environment variables. Create a site configuration file in the root of your project directory, naming it &lt;code>hugo.toml&lt;/code>, &lt;code>hugo.yaml&lt;/code>, or &lt;code>hugo.json&lt;/code>, with that order of precedence.&lt;br>&lt;br>
— &lt;a href="https://gohugo.io/configuration/all/"target="_blank" rel="noopener">Docs &amp;gt; Configuration &amp;gt; All settings (Hugo)&lt;/a>&lt;/p>
&lt;/blockquote>
&lt;div class="hx:overflow-x-auto hx:mt-6 hx:flex hx:flex-col hx:rounded-lg hx:border hx:py-4 hx:px-4 hx:border-gray-200 hx:contrast-more:border-current hx:contrast-more:dark:border-current hx:border-blue-200 hx:bg-blue-100 hx:text-blue-900 hx:dark:border-blue-200/30 hx:dark:bg-blue-900/30 hx:dark:text-blue-200">
